  "raw_text": "29\n\nÂu wiaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto say yes, to confirm, to agree\n \n/ decir sí, confirmar, aceptar\n\nAuas\n \n–\n \nsee/ver:\n \nAwas\n\nAubaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto flow, to stream, to stretch out, to comb, to rake\n... / fluir, estirar, peinar, rastrillar...\n\nAubra\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nstream, rapids, torrent, current\n \n/ corriente, rápidos, torrente\n\n(Construct:\n \nAubriki, Aubrikam, Aubrika\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\nlv135\n):\n \nUpla kum awala kum aubrika ba mapara yawi ba baku, …\n \n–\n \nLike a person swimming against the river\n\ncurrent, …\n \n/ Como una persona que nada contra la corriente de un río, ...)\n\nLî aubra\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nstream of water, flow of water\n \n/ corriente de agua, flujo de agua\n\nLî aubaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto flow, to rise (tide), to pull water, to draw water, to absorb water\n \n/ fluir, subir (marea), sacar\nagua, jalar agua, absorber agua\n\nAudi\n \n–\n \nregards\n \n/ saludos\n\n(Construct:\n \nAudiki\n;\n \nAudikam; Audika\n)\n\n(Note/Nota: an expression of respect, which can be used in writing or verbally / una expresión de respeto, que se puede usar por\nescrito o verbalmente)\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\naem\n):\n \nPamalikam ra audiki yas\n \n–\n \nGive my regards to your family\n \n/ Dale mis saludos a tu familia)\n\nAudi wis\n \n–\n \nsay hi, say goodbye, give my regards\n \n/ di hola, di adiós, dale mis saludos\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\naem\n):\n \nMayam ra audi wis\n \n–\n \nGive my regards to your husband/wife\n \n/ Dale mis saludos a tu esposo/esposa)\n\nAuhaia\n \n(a/t:\n \nAuhwaia\n \nbut is\n \nAuwaia\n \nthe intrans?) (v)\n \n–\n \nto rain, to snow, to hail\n \n/ llover, nevar, granizar\n\nLî auhaia\n \n(&\n \nLî auhwaia\n?) (v)\n \n–\n \nto rain\n \n/ llover\n\n(\nEx/Ej:\n \nLî\n \nauhisa\n \n–\n \nI\nt’s raining\n \n/\n \nE\nstá lloviendo\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej:\n \nNahuala, lî ailal auhwi kan\n \n–\n \nYesterday it was raining a lot\n \n/ Ayer estaba lloviendo mucho)\n\n(Ex/Ej:\n \nlî ba takaskras auhwan\n \n–\n \nit rained without stopping\n \n/ llovió sin parar)\n\n(\nEx/Ej:\n \nlî auhi ba\n \n–\n \nthe raining, the rainstorm\n \n/\n \nla lluvia, la tormenta\n)\n\nL\nî\n \nauhka\n \n(\ndb\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nrain, rainwater\n \n/ lluvia, agua de lluvia\n\nLî auhras\n \n(\ndb,lfb\n) (v-neg,n/s)\n \n–\n \nnot rain, not raining, drought\n \n/ no llueve, sequía\n\n(Ex/Ej:\n \nLî auhras ba\n \n–\n \nthe drought\n \n/ la sequía)\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\nlfb48\n):\n \nLî auhras kan piua ra, Jehova Elías ra win: ...\n \n–\n \nAt the time that it was not raining, Jehovah said to\nElijah: ...\n;\n \nAt the time of the drought, Jehovah said to Elijah: ...\n \n/ En el momento en que no estaba lloviendo,\nJehová le dijo a Elías: ...; En el momento de la sequía, Jehová le dijo a Elías: ...)\n\nAuhbaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto fill, to store, to pack, to load (ex: a boat, truck, car, or a rifle), to stuff\n \n/ llenar, almacenar, empacar,\ncargar (ej: un bote, camión, carro, o un fusil), rellenar\n\nÂiauhbra\n \n(n-agent/s-agente)\n \n–\n \nperson or thing that fills, stores, packs, loads, or stuffs\n \n/ persona o cosa que llena,\nalmacena, empaca, o carga\n\nAuhbaika\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nsomething used to store things, a container\n \n/ algo usado para almacenar cosas, un contenedor\n\nLâ auhbaika watla\n \n(\ndb\n;\n \ndb\n \nalso uses / también usa\n \nLâ auhbaia watla/watlika\n,\n \nlâka auhban watla\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nark of\nthe covenant\n \n/ arca del pacto\n \n(See also/ Ver también:\n \nLâ aisi daukan arkka\n)\n\nAuhn\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ntaste, flavor\n \n/ sabor\n\n(Construct\n:\n \nAuhnka\n)\n\nAuhni\n \n(adj)\n \n–\n \nwith flavor, tasty, d\nelicious, exquisite, nice\n \n/\n \nc\non sabor, sabroso, delicioso, exquisito, agradable\n\nAuhya\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nsand, beach, seashore, coast\n \n/\n \narena, playa,\n \norilla del mar,\n \ncosta\n\nAuhika\n \n(construct of\n/de:\n \nAuhya\n)\n \n–\n \nthe sand, the beach, the seashore, the coast\n \n/\n \nla arena, la playa, la orilla del\n\nmar, la costa\n\nKabu auhika\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nsea sand, sand of the sea\n \n/\n \narena del mar\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\ndb\n-\nAiseya\n \n48:19\n):\n \nkabu auhika baku\n \n–\n \nlike sand of the sea\n \n/\n \ncomo arena del mar\n)\n\nAuhya mâ\n \n(ma)\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ngrain of sand\n \n/ grano de arena\n\nAulala\n \n(\nbc,dict,dictu\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nannatto\n \n/ achiote\n\n(Note\n/Nota\n: a red\n-\ncolored spice and dye\n \n/\n \nuna especia y tinte de color rojo\n)\n\nAula\n \n(v\n-\nirregular\n-\n3p\n-\npres I of\n/de:\n \nBalaia\n)\n \n–\n \n(he/she/it is presently)\n \ncoming\n \n/\n \n(él/ella/ella está actualmente) viniendo\n,\n\nviene\n\n(\nEx/Ej:\n \nL\nî\n \naula\n \n–\n \nrain is (immediately) coming\n \n/\n \nviene la lluvia (inmediatamente)\n)\n\nAulma\n \n(v\n-\nirregular\n-\n2p\n-\npres\n-\nI of\n/de:\n \nBalaia\n)\n \n–\n \n(you are presently)\n \ncom\ning\n \n/\n \n(actualmente) vienes\n\nAulna\n \n(v\n-\ni\nrregular\n-\n1p\n-\npres\n-\nI of\n/de:\n \nverb\n \nBalaia\n)\n \n–\n \n(I am presently)\n \ncom\ning\n \n/\n \n(\ne\nstoy actualmente) vin\niendo\n;\n \nvengo\n\nAuma\n \n(v-irregular-2p-pres-I of/de:\n \nWaia\n)\n \n–\n \n(you are presently) going\n \n/ (actualmente) vas",
